<Layout title="RummyScore Support — Zomsi" description="Support for RummyScore.">
<main class="section"><div class="container legal-copy">
<span class="eyebrow">RummyScore support</span><h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.7rem,6vw,4.8rem);margin-top:18px">How can we help?</h1>
<p class="lead">For support, include your device model, operating system version, RummyScore version, a description of the issue, and steps to reproduce it when possible.</p>
<div class="card"><h3>Contact support</h3><p style="color:var(--muted)">Email us at:</p><a class="button primary" href="mailto:support@zomsi.co">support@zomsi.co</a></div>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Does RummyScore require an internet connection?</h3><p>Core scorekeeping is designed to work without requiring an internet connection.</p>
<h3>What type of Rummy does it support?</h3><p>RummyScore is designed primarily for Indian Rummy scorekeeping.</p>
<h3>Can scoring values be customized?</h3><p>Yes. Game settings can include configurable Target Score, Middle Drop, Wrong Show, and Full Count values.</p>
<h3>Does RummyScore support real-money gaming?</h3><p>No. RummyScore is a scorekeeping utility only and does not provide gambling, betting, wagering, or cash gameplay.</p>
</div></main>
</Layout>
